# Insight: reusable E2E report (`y-ins-e2e-report`)

Use this rule when an E2E or manual-E2E run needs a final report artifact.

This is a shared report contract. Any project's installed E2E entry rule (`y-tst-e2e*`) can invoke it. Invoking project rules add extra required fields for their scenario.

---

## Report artifact policy

- Output **three Markdown report files** per run (always write **1** then **2**; **3** is extra and must not replace them):
  1. **Full report** — complete internal record (local setup, execution detail, issues).
  2. **Compact report** — shareable with other teams; sanitized per [Compact shareable report](#compact-shareable-report) below.
  3. **QA Test Samples report** — QA-aligned paste for Jira **Test Samples** (full test-cases doc coverage, team-facing, no noise); see [QA Test Samples report](#qa-test-samples-report). If that file is skipped (missing test-cases doc and user stops, or user declines), **still keep files 1 and 2**.
- Save all of these report files under **`cursor_workspace/`** (invoking rule can require a specific subdirectory, e.g. `cursor_workspace/ai_test/e2e/`). The QA file uses the **same folder**.
- Do not overwrite previous reports.
- Filename must include **Jira key**, **date + time** as **`YYYYMMDD-HHMM`** (24-hour **local** time when the run finished; minute precision; no separators in the date), and a short scenario slug.
- **Filename pattern:** `E2E-Report-<JIRA>-<YYYYMMDD-HHMM>-<scenario-slug>-report.md` (use `NO-TICKET` when no Jira key).
- Compact file uses the **same basename** as the full report with **`-compact`** immediately before `.md` (for example `E2E-Report-VAP-2325-20260730-1612-leak-check-report-compact.md` when the full file is `E2E-Report-VAP-2325-20260730-1612-leak-check-report.md`).
- QA file uses the **same basename** as the full report with **`-qa`** immediately before `.md` (for example `E2E-Report-VAP-2325-20260730-1612-leak-check-report-qa.md`).
- Write the **full report first**, then produce the **compact report** from it (same facts, sanitized presentation). Then write the **QA** file from those facts plus the test-cases doc (path rules in [QA Test Samples report](#qa-test-samples-report)). Never skip full or compact in order to write QA.
- **Report type** in **Metadata** (Detailed and Compact files only):
  - Full file: exactly **`Detailed`**
  - Compact file: exactly **`Compact`**
  The QA file has **no Metadata** and **no Report type** field.
- If a value is not verified, write **`(not verified)`** explicitly in every report file.

---

## Formatting rules (both reports)

- Any bullet or line that uses a `label: value` pattern must format the label in bold.
- Use this style consistently: `- **Label:** value`.
- Apply this to all report sections, not only the transcript section.
- Keep values unbolded unless another rule explicitly requires emphasis.
- Colons that are part of normal prose (not a `label: value` field) are allowed without bold labels.
- This applies to nested bullets too (for example under verification blocks).
- Do not leave unlabeled continuation lines under transcript or evidence fields.
- If a field value is multiline, either:
  - keep it on one line with explicit `\n` markers, or
  - continue on indented lines under the same bullet without creating a new unlabeled block, or
  - **(required when the value contains Markdown)** put the value in a **fenced code block** (use `text` as the language tag) on the lines immediately after the label.
- **Markdown-in-values rule (mandatory):** when a stored value contains Markdown-formatted text (for example a leading `#`/`##`/`###`/`####` header, `**bold**`, `> blockquote`, list bullets that would re-flow, or backtick fences), you **must** render it inside a fenced ` ```text ` block. Do not paste it inline as bullet text and do not escape characters one by one — the fenced block preserves the value verbatim and prevents the report’s outline from being polluted by embedded headers.
- Choose the smallest block that fits: only wrap the offending value (typically `Content`, `AIReasoning`, `Evidence`), not the whole message group.
- Always announce the block with a labeled bullet that ends with `:`, e.g. `- **Content (verbatim — fenced because the value contains Markdown):**`, then a blank line, then the fenced block.

---

## Document title (both reports)

**Full** and **compact** use the **same H1 pattern**:

```markdown
# E2E Report - VAP-2325 - 20260730-1612 - Reactive leak — resident follow-up E2E
```

**Pattern:** `E2E Report - <jira-ticket-id> - <YYYYMMDD-HHMM> - <scenario>`

| Part | Rule |
|------|------|
| **Prefix** | Literal `E2E Report` |
| **Jira ticket id** | e.g. `VAP-2325`; use `NO-TICKET` when none |
| **Timestamp** | Run finished (or report written), **24-hour local**, format **`YYYYMMDD-HHMM`** (e.g. `20260730-1612`) |
| **Scenario** | Short scenario description (same text in full and compact) |
| **Separators** | ` - ` (space-hyphen-space) between parts |

**Must match filename:** The `<jira-ticket-id>` and `<YYYYMMDD-HHMM>` in the H1 must match the filename (see [Report artifact policy](#report-artifact-policy)).

Place the H1 **before** the **Metadata** section.

