## QA Test Samples report

**Audience:** QA (and anyone filling Jira **Test Samples**).

**Purpose:** a **QA-aligned** view of **`docs/<JIRA-KEY>/test-cases.md`** — **every case in that document**, in the document’s order, with pass/fail (or **Not run**) from this run. Same outcomes as Detailed/Compact, but **team-facing** and **without noise** (no local setup, transcripts, rule paths, or operational detail). Not a transcript dump. Not a replacement for Detailed or Compact.

**Coverage:** mirror the **entire** test-cases document. Use each case’s **code and title from the doc** (for example `TST-BUG-001` when the doc uses that convention — not limited to a `TST-*` prefix). Do **not** cherry-pick a subset of cases for QA.

**Test-cases doc path:** `docs/<JIRA-KEY>/test-cases.md` by default, or the path the invoking rule or the user chose (for example `docs/tickets/<JIRA-KEY>/test-cases.md`). The rest of this section calls it the test-cases doc.

**When:** after the full and compact files exist. Source cases **only** from that test-cases doc (same order as the doc).

If the test-cases doc is **missing:** **AskQuestion** — continue without the QA file / stop QA file only. **Do not** invent case codes. **Do not** skip or delete Detailed and Compact.

**Filename and title:**

- File: same basename as the full report with **`-qa`** immediately before `.md`.
- H1: same pattern as [Document title (both reports)](#document-title-both-reports), then ` - QA` at the end.
- **No `## Metadata` section** and **no `Report type` field** in this file. Filename `-qa.md` is enough. Detailed and Compact **keep** their Metadata (including `Detailed` / `Compact`).

**After H1 (plain bullets, no heading):**

- **Environment:** team-facing (same compact sanitization)
- **Overall:** pass / fail / partial
- **Counts:** passed / failed / not run (over **all** cases in the test-cases doc)
- **Cases covered:** one bullet per case in doc order: code, title, Pass / Fail / Not run

Do **not** include **Work item** or **Source** (path to test-cases.md). The H1 already has the Jira key. QA does not need the local doc path.

**Per test case (required — every case in the test-cases doc, same order; keep each block short):**

```markdown
### <Case code> — <Title>

- **Goal:** <one short line from the test-cases doc>
- **Setup / Prerequisites:** <one line: env, data, role; or none>
- **Pass/Fail:** Pass | Fail | Not run
- **Expected vs observed:** <one line>
```

Use the **case code and title exactly as in the test-cases doc** (heading `### …`). Setup: one line, quality bar from `.cursor/rules/y-rules/test/y-tst-test-case.mdc` (env, data, role). Write **`none`** only when honest. Team-facing only (no localhost, Docker, compose, rule-file paths, secrets).

**Omit (noise):** `## Metadata`, Report type, **Work item**, **Source**, transcripts, images, WO dumps, What was executed, Issues/next actions, Docker, localhost, `.mdc` paths, secrets. Do **not** paste full test-cases.md steps.

Cases executed in this run that are **not** in the test-cases doc: omit here (they stay in Detailed/Compact only). **Every** case in the test-cases doc must appear in the QA file; cases that were **not** executed in this run: **Not run**.

